WEBVTT

00:02.230 --> 00:05.230
The changing room is 
way too far from the venue...

00:05.890 --> 00:10.570
<i>Maybe it's careless to attend a cosplay 
event in the same town where I work.</i>

00:11.320 --> 00:14.240
<i>Well, considering all the foot traffic,</i>

00:14.240 --> 00:17.370
<i>and that it's in the opposite direction from 
the office, and it's a day off...</i>

00:15.490 --> 00:17.740
<b>Cosplay Event Reception
On the Left</b>

00:18.630 --> 00:20.640
<i>I doubt I'll run into anyone.</i>

00:20.640 --> 00:22.650
Huh? Hayakawa-san?

00:23.250 --> 00:26.150
What a coincidence, 
running into you on a day off.

00:26.770 --> 00:27.750
What's up?

00:36.290 --> 00:39.340
<i>My name is Hayakawa Chinatsu, 22 years old...</i>

00:39.930 --> 00:42.520
<i>I'm an office worker in my 
first year of employment.</i>

00:44.180 --> 00:48.300
<i>And my boss just found out 
about me being an otaku.</i>

00:49.450 --> 00:56.130
<i>Oh, I love you so much, I just have to laugh</i>

01:00.990 --> 01:05.750
My Tiny Senpai

01:06.500 --> 01:08.830
<i>We've got an emergency here</i>

01:09.250 --> 01:11.610
<i>Are you paying attention, me?</i>

01:12.000 --> 01:17.840
<i>There's someone other than me 
dancing around inside of my heart</i>

01:17.840 --> 01:20.090
<i>I want to talk to her</i>

01:20.600 --> 01:23.140
<i>I want to touch her</i>

01:23.140 --> 01:28.630
<i>Look, I get it, but for now try to pipe down</i>

01:29.150 --> 01:31.860
<i>What in the world am I doing?</i>

01:31.860 --> 01:34.610
<i>You're right next to me</i>

01:34.610 --> 01:40.860
<i>And this is the perfect chance...</i>

01:41.620 --> 01:42.440
<i>HONEY</i>

01:42.440 --> 01:47.150
<i>I'm trapped by that sweet rich taste</i>

01:47.150 --> 01:50.360
<i>And I don't think I can ever escape</i>

01:50.360 --> 01:52.860
<i>I may as well just sink into it</i>

01:52.860 --> 01:53.670
<i>HONEY</i>

01:53.670 --> 01:58.470
<i>It's another day in your dazzling presence</i>

01:58.680 --> 02:01.470
<i>We may never be 
on the same page with this love but</i>

02:01.470 --> 02:07.900
<i>Oh, I love you so much, I just have to laugh</i>

02:19.490 --> 02:23.490
#04 When It Comes to Him, I'm Not Sure Yet...

02:21.350 --> 02:23.490
What are you up to, Hayakawa-san?

02:27.250 --> 02:31.710
Y-You've got the wrong person! 
I-I'm not Hayakawa, Manager!

02:31.710 --> 02:33.500
You just called me your manager.

02:33.500 --> 02:35.880
<b>Cosplay Event Reception
On the Left</b>

02:33.790 --> 02:35.880
<i>Of all the people...</i>

02:36.480 --> 02:42.140
<i>The manager is like the textbook 
definition of a normie, too!</i>

02:44.720 --> 02:48.770
Huh. A cosplay event? I see.

02:49.520 --> 02:50.540
Hayakawa-san.

02:50.540 --> 02:51.770
Y-Yes?

02:51.770 --> 02:54.550
Where do you buy an outfit like that?

02:54.550 --> 02:58.630
W-Well, I-I actually made it myself.

02:59.780 --> 03:01.280
<i>I'm done.</i>

03:01.280 --> 03:03.100
<i>It's all over for me...</i>

03:03.100 --> 03:05.260
<i>He's probably wondering 
why a grown woman is doing</i>

03:05.260 --> 03:07.290
<i>something like this and thinks it's creepy.</i>

03:08.850 --> 03:10.790
I have to say, Hayakawa-san...

03:10.790 --> 03:13.150
<i>Here it comes! The words every otaku dreads!</i>

03:13.150 --> 03:16.300
<i>I don't wanna hear it! I don't wanna 
hear my manager call me creepy!</i>

03:16.720 --> 03:19.920
That's pretty cool, Hayakawa-san.

03:21.680 --> 03:24.460
It is?

03:24.460 --> 03:26.930
Yeah. I think it's really cool.

03:31.940 --> 03:35.690
Wait, how?! What about this is cool?

03:35.690 --> 03:36.880
Your approach to life, maybe?

03:36.880 --> 03:38.320
A-All that?!

03:38.320 --> 03:40.300
I don't have any hobbies,

03:40.300 --> 03:45.480
so I respect people who do, 
like you. I think it's pretty cool.

03:49.660 --> 03:52.730
Then again, that outfit 
is more cute than cool.

03:54.820 --> 03:58.210
<i>How can he just up and say 
something like that?!</i>

03:59.410 --> 04:00.270
What's wrong?

04:00.270 --> 04:02.970
N-Nothing, th-thank you.

04:04.010 --> 04:07.640
Manager! Please don't tell anyone about this.

04:08.390 --> 04:10.190
Is it supposed to be a secret?

04:10.190 --> 04:11.520
Please!

04:11.520 --> 04:13.770
But it's really impressive.

04:13.770 --> 04:16.420
That's a matter of opinion.

04:16.420 --> 04:17.770
A-Anyway...

04:17.770 --> 04:23.280
Let's keep this a secret, 
just between us. Please.

04:25.960 --> 04:27.040
Cute!

04:27.040 --> 04:29.320
Why would you say it again?!

04:29.320 --> 04:30.540
Well...

04:30.940 --> 04:35.010
The first one was more about 
your costume and how you look,

04:35.010 --> 04:38.420
and the second one was more about 
you personally, Hayakawa-san.

04:40.940 --> 04:43.120
I didn't want an actual explanation!

04:43.120 --> 04:45.930
I didn't hear anything 
you just said! Not a thing!

04:45.930 --> 04:48.170
But it's true that you're—

04:48.170 --> 04:49.530
Like! I! Said!

04:49.530 --> 04:53.620
I heard nothing!

04:56.690 --> 04:58.690
I love you.

05:01.240 --> 05:05.490
<i>The deadline for Comiket 
submissions is coming up...</i>

05:05.720 --> 05:07.990
<i>But I can't focus.</i>

05:08.470 --> 05:12.550
<i>I can't believe my boss 
found out that I'm a cosplayer.</i>

05:12.550 --> 05:16.890
<i>I asked him to keep quiet, 
and I doubt he'd blab, but...</i>

05:17.770 --> 05:20.670
<i>I wonder if there's a pressure point 
to erase someone's memory...</i>

05:20.670 --> 05:23.010
Where am I? What are you?

05:24.240 --> 05:26.570
How did this even happen?

05:26.570 --> 05:30.760
Work is going to be a nightmare tomorrow.

05:32.640 --> 05:33.390
Senpai!

05:33.990 --> 05:37.640
I'd like you to review the materials I put 
together for the upcoming project submission.

05:37.640 --> 05:39.900
Sure! I'll take a look.

05:39.900 --> 05:41.390
Let's see here...

05:41.390 --> 05:45.100
Yep, you covered 
your bases nicely! Well done.

05:45.100 --> 05:46.970
Th-Thank you.

05:46.970 --> 05:49.520
<i>Didn't get anywhere with my manuscript...</i>

05:49.520 --> 05:50.920
<i>Didn't sleep much...</i>

05:50.920 --> 05:52.610
<i>This really sucks...</i>

05:52.610 --> 05:55.910
Hayakawa. Hey, Hayakawa?

05:56.660 --> 05:59.640
You okay? You look worn out.

05:59.640 --> 06:02.290
Oh, er, I-I'm totally fine!

06:02.880 --> 06:06.970
It's just, a bunch of stuff happened 
yesterday... and I didn't get much sleep.

06:07.320 --> 06:10.000
A lack of sleep can contribute 
to all kinds of health problems.

06:10.000 --> 06:11.640
Be careful, okay?

06:12.120 --> 06:15.880
When you can't sleep, try counting cats!

06:15.880 --> 06:17.500
One kitty,

06:17.500 --> 06:19.100
two kitties,

06:19.100 --> 06:20.760
three kitties,

06:20.070 --> 06:22.760
I think most people use sheep...

06:20.760 --> 06:22.580
four kitties—

06:23.380 --> 06:25.610
No! Cats are fine, too.

06:26.760 --> 06:29.190
Thanks for the concern, Katase-san.

06:29.600 --> 06:30.790
Hayakawa-san...

06:31.690 --> 06:33.910
Are you not feeling well? Everything okay?

06:34.190 --> 06:35.540
M-Manager?!

06:35.820 --> 06:40.790
Uh, well... er... yes, I-I'm okay.

06:41.050 --> 06:45.800
Okay. In that case, would you like to 
join me for dinner tonight?

06:46.600 --> 06:48.520
I was hoping we could talk.

06:49.350 --> 06:51.160
In a nice, quiet restaurant.

06:51.960 --> 06:53.300
Just the two of us,
if that's all right.

06:53.300 --> 06:57.560
<i>Dinner for j-just the two of us?! 
You mean like...</i>

06:57.560 --> 07:01.480
<i>Cute... Cute... Cute...{repeat as necessary}</i>

07:02.560 --> 07:04.350
W-Well...

07:04.820 --> 07:07.230
a-as long as we're done before the last train.

07:07.230 --> 07:08.420
Sounds great.

07:08.880 --> 07:11.210
Let me know when
you're done work.

07:12.680 --> 07:13.540
Okay.

07:14.290 --> 07:15.400
Is this a date?

07:15.400 --> 07:16.740
I-It isn't!

07:16.740 --> 07:18.000
Sounds suspicious!

07:18.000 --> 07:19.870
Well, it's not!

07:21.440 --> 07:22.320
<i>Right.</i>

07:22.910 --> 07:25.590
<i>This isn't a date or anything like that.</i>

07:28.920 --> 07:33.220
<i>My boss just... asked me out... 
for a bit of dinner.</i>

07:34.710 --> 07:35.930
<i>It's nothing.</i>

07:36.660 --> 07:38.220
<i>It's not a big deal!</i>

07:40.950 --> 07:42.460
Sorry about the wait.

07:49.650 --> 07:50.570
You okay?

07:50.570 --> 07:52.980
W-Well... er...

07:53.900 --> 07:55.630
Thanks for the save.

07:55.630 --> 07:58.720
Don't mention it. Watch your step, now.

07:58.720 --> 07:59.370
Okay.

07:59.680 --> 08:04.500
Speaking of... when you came for your 
employment test, didn't you break a heel?

08:05.540 --> 08:08.130
You remember that?

08:08.130 --> 08:10.260
Of course I do.

08:14.040 --> 08:16.260
That must've been rough.

08:16.670 --> 08:21.770
But I'm glad you passed, 
and now we get to work together.

08:21.770 --> 08:23.620
<i>He remembered...</i>

08:24.880 --> 08:27.020
Now, let's get a move on, Hayakawa-san.

08:27.020 --> 08:28.270
O-Okay.

08:31.200 --> 08:34.640
I'd think you're used to the office by now,

08:34.640 --> 08:37.240
but do you have any issues 
or things you're worried about?

08:37.240 --> 08:41.260
No. Everyone is really nice, 
so nothing comes to mind.

08:41.260 --> 08:43.320
Well, that's good to hear.

08:43.320 --> 08:45.340
The section chief mentioned 
how impressed he was

08:45.340 --> 08:46.930
with how much faster you've gotten.

08:46.930 --> 08:49.130
Come on, it's nothing that impressive.

08:50.640 --> 08:54.220
<i>All he's brought up 
during dinner is work stuff,</i>

08:54.220 --> 08:57.140
<i>so I guess this is more like 
a dinner meeting than anything.</i>

08:58.100 --> 09:02.250
Manager, didn't you mention 
something you wanted to discuss?

09:03.090 --> 09:04.140
Right.

09:05.510 --> 09:07.150
Hayakawa-san...

09:07.670 --> 09:11.390
I know this might surprise you 
coming out of the blue, but...

09:15.920 --> 09:17.410
Hayakawa-san...

09:18.080 --> 09:22.440
when I look at you, I got really excited.

09:24.900 --> 09:27.500
I've never felt this way before,

09:28.190 --> 09:31.420
and I'm not sure if it's fair 
to spring this on you...

09:32.210 --> 09:37.320
<i>Hang on... is this... is he...?!</i>

09:39.430 --> 09:40.430
Hayakawa-san!

09:40.720 --> 09:42.510
Y-Yes?!

09:43.910 --> 09:47.020
I'd like to attend a cosplay event with you!

09:49.900 --> 09:52.590
I mean, when I think about 
how you made that costume,

09:52.590 --> 09:55.500
I get excited thinking about 
how much fun it must be!

09:55.500 --> 09:57.030
That's what you meant?!

09:57.030 --> 10:00.840
Well... are you saying you 
want to cosplay, too, Manager?

10:00.840 --> 10:03.770
Nope. When I went home 
and started looking into it,

10:03.770 --> 10:07.500
I found out about photo sessions 
they have for cosplay, and well...

10:08.420 --> 10:10.440
I'd love to capture your exploits with this!

10:10.440 --> 10:13.050
<i>What a scary combo of initiative 
and purchasing power!</i>

10:13.440 --> 10:17.240
I-I mean, you could just take pictures 
of whatever cosplay you want.

10:17.640 --> 10:19.470
You don't need me for that...

10:19.470 --> 10:23.620
But you were the one who made me 
realize it'd be fun, Hayakawa-san.

10:24.430 --> 10:27.080
I want it to be you.

10:30.160 --> 10:34.070
<i>It's not fair how he can just say stuff 
like that with a straight face...</i>

10:36.150 --> 10:37.460
The month after next,

10:39.120 --> 10:43.640
there's going to be an event 
at the same location, so if you want...

10:44.570 --> 10:49.440
Oh, but in exchange, you need the check out 
the things my costumes are from!

10:48.870 --> 10:51.830
<b>Real otaku always proselytize</b>

10:49.440 --> 10:51.830
Otherwise you can't take pictures!

10:53.640 --> 10:54.680
Cute.

10:54.680 --> 10:55.980
How?!

10:55.980 --> 10:57.840
None of that was cute at all!

10:57.840 --> 11:01.400
Yes, it was. The way you're so earnest 
about talking about the things you like.

11:01.400 --> 11:02.560
It was very c—

11:02.560 --> 11:04.510
No more explanations!

11:04.510 --> 11:05.720
But you're the one who was—

11:05.720 --> 11:09.150
I do not want to hear it at all! 
Not another word!

11:13.360 --> 11:15.870
Shinozaki, you wanna grab lunch?

11:15.870 --> 11:18.890
Sure. Let me just finish this up.

11:18.890 --> 11:19.830
Got it.

11:21.320 --> 11:22.240
You need to talk?

11:23.780 --> 11:26.240
Well... yeah.

11:28.270 --> 11:30.360
Okay, one sec. I'll be right there.

11:30.980 --> 11:32.620
I'll wait in the lobby.

11:32.620 --> 11:37.550
Y'know, Hayakawa-san and Shinozaki-kun 
seem closer than regular coworkers.

11:37.550 --> 11:40.750
Apparently, they're childhood friends 
who grew up as neighbors.

11:40.750 --> 11:43.110
Oh, right. I remember 
hearing about that, now.

11:43.890 --> 11:47.080
Are you interested in what's going on?

11:47.080 --> 11:49.210
Katase-san, there's no need to get giddy.

11:49.210 --> 11:52.640
Since you always pick on me, 
I'm just glad for a chance at payback!

11:53.050 --> 11:58.550
Hayakawa-san might've denied it before, 
but maybe there is actually a chance...

11:59.400 --> 12:03.280
m 0 0 l 118 0 l 118 168 l 0 168

11:59.400 --> 12:03.280
<b>Or the
reunited
childhood
friends/
classmates
romance.</b>

12:00.600 --> 12:03.280
A reunited childhood 
friends/classmates romance.

12:03.280 --> 12:06.660
m 0 0 l 118 0 l 118 166 l 0 166

12:03.280 --> 12:06.660
<b>The age-gap
romance
between
a senpai
and kohai
at work.</b>

12:04.200 --> 12:06.660
An age-gap romance 
between a senpai and kohai at work.

12:06.660 --> 12:10.100
Which one am I supposed to root for?!

12:10.100 --> 12:13.290
Sh-Sh-Shinozaki-san and I aren't like that...

12:13.290 --> 12:14.920
More importantly, Manager!

12:15.180 --> 12:18.550
Aren't you forgetting an option?

12:18.550 --> 12:20.800
Another option...?

12:20.800 --> 12:24.480
There's nothing like another girl.

12:24.480 --> 12:26.650
H-Hayakawa-san...

12:26.650 --> 12:28.030
Of course.

12:28.030 --> 12:30.060
Why would you take it that way?!

12:30.060 --> 12:33.020
You brought it up, Katase-san,

12:33.020 --> 12:36.840
but aren't you curious about what's going on 
with Shinozaki-kun and Hayakawa-san?

12:37.400 --> 12:41.610
N-Not really. The two of them 
can be as friendly as they want...

12:41.610 --> 12:45.660
B-Besides, why would I care?

12:45.660 --> 12:47.680
I dunno, why would you?

12:47.680 --> 12:50.910
Aw! Don't answer a question 
with another question!

12:51.200 --> 12:54.990
Come on, we better hurry before 
the lunch crowds fill everywhere up!

12:54.990 --> 12:56.270
But why would you?!

12:56.270 --> 12:57.420
Manager!

12:59.930 --> 13:02.200
The manager found out you're an otaku?

13:02.200 --> 13:03.510
I got careless.

13:03.890 --> 13:05.180
How'd that even happen?

13:05.730 --> 13:07.580
Did he see something you were drawing...?

13:07.580 --> 13:10.430
Not exactly.

13:11.090 --> 13:15.190
<i>Shinozaki knows I'm an otaku, 
but not about the cosplay stuff.</i>

13:15.560 --> 13:19.310
I don't really think him knowing 
is a problem, though.

13:20.040 --> 13:23.570
Well... maybe not a big problem...

13:24.500 --> 13:26.250
Not a serious one, but...

13:26.570 --> 13:29.570
Cute... Cute... Cute...

13:31.740 --> 13:33.870
If it's not a problem, then what's the issue?

13:33.870 --> 13:34.830
You're right.

13:35.570 --> 13:38.700
I guess I should be glad 
he didn't see me drawing BL dojinshi.

13:38.700 --> 13:40.170
Whacha talking about?

13:40.170 --> 13:41.460
M-Manager?!

13:42.050 --> 13:44.460
<i>Did he hear all that?!</i>

13:45.190 --> 13:47.340
Are you here for lunch with Senpai?

13:47.340 --> 13:49.210
Are you curious?

13:49.210 --> 13:53.600
Not exactly... and why are you 
grinning like that?

13:53.600 --> 13:56.730
Do you mind if 
we join you for lunch?

13:56.730 --> 13:58.480
Oh, sure.

13:58.480 --> 14:02.480
In that case, I wanna sit 
next to Hayakawa-san!

14:04.100 --> 14:05.230
Don't let it bug you.

14:05.230 --> 14:07.490
What is up with you today?!

14:07.800 --> 14:10.080
I wonder what I should get.

14:10.080 --> 14:11.690
I'm curious, Hayakawa-san.

14:13.400 --> 14:14.970
What's BL?

14:15.960 --> 14:19.560
W-Well, it's, er... it is sort of a...

14:20.190 --> 14:24.070
What's wrong, Hayakawa-san? 
You've gone bright red.

14:25.220 --> 14:27.010
I-I-I wonder why.

14:27.680 --> 14:30.780
Is it okay if I make this picture 
my home screen background?

14:30.780 --> 14:32.070
Of course not!

14:34.160 --> 14:37.400
<i>My Tiny Senpai</i>.

14:40.710 --> 14:42.380
Shinozaki-san!

14:45.230 --> 14:50.240
Trick or treat! 
Happy Halloween, Shinozaki-san!

14:50.640 --> 14:51.980
Senpai!

14:53.240 --> 14:55.790
It's Halloween, after all.

14:55.790 --> 14:56.670
What do you think?

14:56.680 --> 14:59.920
It's cu—er, very nice looking.

14:59.920 --> 15:01.820
I was kinda surprised.

15:01.820 --> 15:05.750
That being the case, 
once again: trick or treat!

15:06.640 --> 15:10.260
S-Sorry, I didn't get anything ready...

15:11.350 --> 15:12.830
That's okay.

15:12.830 --> 15:14.260
Here you go!

15:15.040 --> 15:16.410
Oh, thank yo—

15:26.390 --> 15:30.030
T-Trick or treat?

15:30.030 --> 15:32.530
Well done! Here you go.

15:32.930 --> 15:34.700
Come on, don't treat me like a kid.

15:33.360 --> 15:37.450
What are you grinning about? 
And with cat ears on.

15:34.700 --> 15:36.600
Which one would you like?

15:38.410 --> 15:42.040
Just thinking how this is going to be 
one sugary Halloween!

15:42.800 --> 15:44.730
By the way, Hayakawa-san.

15:46.420 --> 15:48.000
Happy Halloween!

15:48.420 --> 15:52.260
Yep, I was right. Your cat-like 
nature makes it a good fit.

15:52.680 --> 15:54.170
And we match!

15:54.170 --> 15:57.260
M-Manager! Wearing cat ears at work is...

15:57.430 --> 16:00.270
<b>*Can't bring herself to take them off</b>

16:03.160 --> 16:05.770
The trick to happiness is a bowl of candy!

16:05.770 --> 16:07.850
I love Halloween!

16:07.850 --> 16:09.530
It's pretty great.

16:10.260 --> 16:13.130
It's not a good idea to 
overindulge on sweets, though.

16:13.130 --> 16:15.780
Right! It can cause all kinds of problems.

16:15.780 --> 16:19.150
But it's Halloween, so what can you do?

16:19.150 --> 16:20.810
True.

16:20.810 --> 16:25.280
That also applies to Christmas, Valentine's, 
birthdays, and Hinamatsuri.

16:25.280 --> 16:26.680
Agreed!

16:26.680 --> 16:28.420
<i>That's a lot of exceptions!</i>

16:29.060 --> 16:30.920
Senpai, did you try these chocolates?

16:31.760 --> 16:33.870
Not yet.

16:33.870 --> 16:36.180
They're pretty good. 
They've got a more mature taste.

16:37.460 --> 16:39.180
A mature taste?

16:44.040 --> 16:46.010
<i>I-Is she...?</i>

16:47.300 --> 16:50.900
<i>Sh-She's waiting for me to 
feed her the chocolate?</i>

16:51.200 --> 16:53.160
<i>But if I do that...</i>

16:53.650 --> 17:00.160
<i>M-My finger might touch Senpai's mouth!</i>

17:04.160 --> 17:06.040
<i>But a chance like this...</i>

17:11.970 --> 17:12.840
Yoink.

17:13.840 --> 17:17.080
Too bad. Time's up.

17:21.200 --> 17:22.300
Yummy!

17:24.520 --> 17:27.500
<i>I'm so stupid! I wasted my chance!</i>

17:27.500 --> 17:29.080
Shinozaki-san...

17:30.350 --> 17:35.860
I-I feel weirdly toasty now.

17:37.550 --> 17:40.240
Shinozaki, is there any candy left?

17:40.240 --> 17:43.240
Hayakawa-shan! Hayakawa-shan!

17:46.500 --> 17:49.230
Smooch! Smooch! Smooch!

17:47.920 --> 17:49.660
What's going on with Katase-san?

17:49.230 --> 17:50.860
Don't go!

17:49.660 --> 17:52.550
She just had one of these chocolates...

17:52.550 --> 17:53.510
Chocolate?

17:53.890 --> 17:56.010
Oh, these have alcohol in them.

17:56.280 --> 17:59.420
Who could get that drunk off 
of one chocolate?

18:00.010 --> 18:01.670
Smooooch!

18:00.010 --> 18:02.760
Would someone please help me?!

18:02.760 --> 18:04.440
Who would've guessed that 
Katase-san would turn

18:04.440 --> 18:06.120
into a kissing machine
when she gets drunk?

18:06.120 --> 18:07.640
A kissing machine...

18:07.640 --> 18:10.120
<i>Does that mean I've got a chance?!</i>

18:10.120 --> 18:11.780
Shinozaki-san...

18:12.520 --> 18:16.030
Uh, well, I—I wasn't thinking 
anything naughty!

18:16.030 --> 18:17.280
<i>Stare...</i>

18:17.280 --> 18:19.280
Could you at least say something?

18:21.030 --> 18:23.030
Sorry, sorry!

18:21.030 --> 18:23.030
Is that...

18:23.030 --> 18:24.990
Manager! Manager!

18:26.460 --> 18:27.610
Manager...

18:27.610 --> 18:29.420
To be honest, I...

18:29.420 --> 18:32.900
There's something I need to tell you.

18:34.340 --> 18:37.440
Senpai! Senpai! Our manager 
doesn't photosynthesize.

18:37.440 --> 18:38.840
Over there, see?

18:39.930 --> 18:41.880
I'm right over here!

18:41.880 --> 18:42.930
What's up?

18:42.930 --> 18:44.930
Manager! Manager!

18:45.260 --> 18:51.370
Manager... the truth is, there's 
something I need to tell you...

18:51.920 --> 18:53.820
Wait, is this going where I think it is?!

18:54.110 --> 18:56.610
Are Senpai... and Manager going to...

18:56.610 --> 18:58.820
K-K-K-Kiss?!

19:01.970 --> 19:03.400
Manager...

19:05.580 --> 19:08.080
No! Hold on, Senpai!

19:12.130 --> 19:16.040
I am so, so grateful for the way that you 
always, always work so hard for us,

19:16.040 --> 19:18.190
and to get our work done!

19:18.190 --> 19:19.630
<i>She's bowing out of gratitude?!</i>

19:20.840 --> 19:23.370
Maybe it's less about kissing

19:23.370 --> 19:26.660
and more about her emotions 
towards people getting amplified?

19:25.140 --> 19:29.460
Oh bless you, bless you, God and Manager!

19:28.390 --> 19:31.000
Th-That might be it.

19:31.000 --> 19:33.900
<i>I'm partly glad, and partly disappointed...</i>

19:33.900 --> 19:37.960
Now, then, Katase-senpai, 
your kohai's right over there.

19:38.680 --> 19:39.900
My kohai?

19:40.490 --> 19:42.910
Kohai, Kohai!

19:42.910 --> 19:46.410
<i>Hang on! Finding out 
how she feels about me...</i>

19:46.410 --> 19:48.680
<i>I-I'm not emotionally prepared for this!</i>

19:49.410 --> 19:52.670
U-Uh, Senpai, I...

19:59.550 --> 20:00.800
Wha...?!

20:02.920 --> 20:04.300
Tears?!

20:04.300 --> 20:08.330
I-I'm so sorry! I know I'm always 
causing trouble for you, Senpai!

20:08.330 --> 20:09.560
It's not that.

20:10.030 --> 20:13.280
You used to have no idea 
what to do on your own,

20:13.280 --> 20:16.280
but you're so capable now...

20:16.280 --> 20:19.070
It makes me really happy, as your senpai!

20:19.070 --> 20:20.820
<i>So she's my mom?</i>

20:20.820 --> 20:22.070
But...

20:22.550 --> 20:27.330
if you do need help, 
you can always turn to me, okay?

20:27.680 --> 20:29.750
S-Senpai...

20:30.330 --> 20:34.510
I-I think I'm gonna get you some water! 
You sit here and wait a sec!

20:31.890 --> 20:33.060
Tasty.

20:34.510 --> 20:36.080
'Kay!

20:35.400 --> 20:36.080
Nice.

20:38.840 --> 20:41.210
<i>So Senpai thinks...</i>

20:41.550 --> 20:44.720
You used to have no idea 
what to do on your own...

20:46.520 --> 20:49.470
<i>I'm a little disappointed, 
but I'm still glad.</i>

20:51.170 --> 20:52.860
Katase-san, Katase-san.

20:54.310 --> 20:58.980
What do you think about Shinozaki-kun 
personally, and not as a coworker?

21:01.990 --> 21:04.060
Senpai, I've got your water.

21:04.060 --> 21:05.740
Shinozaki-san is...

21:07.400 --> 21:13.200
When it comes to him... I'm not sure yet...

21:16.620 --> 21:18.570
I thought I had her that time.

21:18.570 --> 21:21.500
Never mind that! Could you 
please delete that picture?

21:22.200 --> 21:23.420
Which one do you mean?

21:23.420 --> 21:25.960
The one with Katase-san and I... y'know...

21:25.960 --> 21:26.870
This one?

21:27.280 --> 21:29.280
Hurry up and delete it!

21:29.280 --> 21:30.750
Can I use it on my home screen?

21:30.750 --> 21:32.470
Of course not!

21:46.260 --> 21:50.140
<i>Bleary-eyed and not fully awake from a dream</i>

21:50.140 --> 21:55.040
<i>I still can't bring myself 
to drink that bitter coffee</i>

21:55.600 --> 21:59.520
<i>So I sneakily toss in 
two pinches of a sweet secret</i>

21:59.520 --> 22:03.740
<i>And let it slowly spread throughout</i>

22:04.960 --> 22:08.700
<i>There's a local bakery 
that's only open sometimes</i>

22:08.700 --> 22:13.590
<i>Where I once had some toast that glittered</i>

22:14.250 --> 22:18.090
<i>What is it that makes it so satisfying?</i>

22:18.090 --> 22:22.260
<i>Almost like magic</i>

22:22.680 --> 22:27.340
<i>I find myself thinking about that kind of thing</i>

22:27.340 --> 22:33.030
<i>How the small things can be the most precious</i>

22:33.790 --> 22:37.740
<i>Deep inside my heart</i>

22:37.740 --> 22:42.140
<i>It's ever so bittersweet</i>

22:43.010 --> 22:47.130
<i>"Just being around you is enough"</i>

22:47.130 --> 22:51.080
<i>Becomes my mantra</i>

22:51.080 --> 22:53.370
<i>Baby like sugar</i>

23:00.560 --> 23:02.700
<i>Baby you're the sugar</i>
